@* The gate every page shows while the card data is still being read.

   Fifteen pages had this as `<p class="p-4">`, character for character. Two things were wrong
   with it repeated rather than shared. The padding is flat, so on a notched phone in landscape
   the message sat under the cutout while every other block on the page cleared it; and it was
   announced to nobody, so a screen reader arriving at a page mid-load found what looked like an
   empty page and no indication that anything was coming.

   Polite rather than assertive: it is the ordinary state of arriving, not something to interrupt
   for. *@

<PageShell>
    <p class="mb-0" role="status">Loading card data&hellip;</p>
</PageShell>
